WEBVTT

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.190
Come on, eat.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.310
Eat it and you’ll be flying off to heaven!

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.870
Heaven, huh?

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:09.320
If I can meet Father...

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.870
I have to apologize...

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.270
about what happened that day.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.820
Then...

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.490
I’m going to dig in!

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:20.790
<b>Chomp</b>

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.430
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.350
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.600
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.940
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.320
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.200
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:16.840
Japan at the apex
of the world!?
Pierrot crosses
the sands of time!!

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.840
Pierrot crosses the sands of time!!

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.600
<i>Japan</i> at the apex of the world!?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:21.990
Japan at the apex
of the world!?
Pierrot crosses
the sands of time!!

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.370
Wh-Who are you?!

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.120
F-Father?!

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.750
Where the hell did you come from?!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.130
Who the hell are you?!

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.250
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.210
It’s me!

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.300
Did you forget about me, Father?

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.510
Father?!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.260
I do not have a big child like you!

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.970
Th-This can’t be...

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.220
My child is still within my queen’s stomach.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.270
Huh? Wh-What does... that mean?

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.490
Now that I look closely, this isn’t heaven.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.150
This is the Royal Palace!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.950
And somehow I get the feeling that it’s kinda new...

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:00.490
F-Father...

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.400
I mean, Your Majesty...

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.110
I’d like to ask you something silly, but...

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.280
What year is this?

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.080
Are you quite all right?

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.420
This is 1982.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.780
1982?!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.250
Why?

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.710
Why did I end up being sent
into the past instead of heaven?

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.050
Darling...

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.590
What’s wrong?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:27.020
I could hear you shouting down the hallway.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.520
M-Mother?!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.600
Oh? And this is...?

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.520
We have a guest?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.890
How could someone like this be a guest?!

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.150
Summon the guards!

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.530
Capture this thief!

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.030
T-Thief?

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.530
Th-This is bad...

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.490
Stop that, Your Majesty!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.540
I’m Pierrot of Quedam Circus.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.830
Pierrot?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.040
Oh, quit pretending.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.250
Your Majesty called me to
entertain your beloved queen, right?

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.250
Oh, is that so?

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.800
Darling...

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.130
Thank you.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.590
I’m sure our soon-to-be-born child will be happy, too.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.760
Is... Is that so?

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.300
That’s right.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:11.770
Let me show you proof that I’m a genuine clown.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:12.600
Starting with...

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.820
a face-stand!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.530
Manager...

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.900
Pierrot hasn’t moved since he ate the bread...

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.410
Can he go to heaven in that state?

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.500
Dunno.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.250
There’s no mistaking it.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.210
He’s gone to heaven with my <i>Japan</i> #61.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:39.750
Right about now all three of them
ought to be in the middle of a joyful reunion.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.960
This has turned into something crazy.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.850
I’m really happy that my dream of meeting both my father and mother has been fulfilled.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.350
But, just how much longer must
I continue fooling them like this?

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.640
Oh, that’s good!

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.850
That’s amazing!

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:07.620
Furthermore, why did I end up
traveling 23 years back in time?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:09.780
Time travel?!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.740
I see!

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.120
Cannabis <i>Japan</i>!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.950
Also known as Hemp <i>Japan</i>!

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.630
It’s a time machine!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.720
The mystery behind Azuma’s bread is that

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.970
it worked as a time machine and sent me into the past!

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.680
Many days have passed since then.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:33.750
I’ve been living in the Royal Palace as Pierrot, the Queen of Monaco’s favorite servant.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.020
It’s a lot of fun to interact with the people of this age.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.270
Just kidding.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.730
Another one! A Pierrot joke!

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.780
But it’s a little annoying.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:48.700
And more than anything else, I was really happy being able to live with my parents.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.110
Pierrot!

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.610
Where are you, Pierrot?

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.040
Coming!

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.870
Pierrot!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.790
Where are you, Pierrot?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.540
I’ve been in front of you for a while.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.290
Oh, really?

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.550
Mother...

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.050
She’s grown so fat, she can’t even open her eyes.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.630
Pierrot...

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.930
Thank you for always entertaining me.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.850
In gratitude, I’d like you to have this ring.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.560
Thank you very much.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.350
Is it really all right?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.770
There’s no need for reservations.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.150
That ring has become too small for me.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.650
It no longer suits my fingers.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.900
It’s not like the ring got small, you know...

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.410
It’s just that all your fingers have turned into thumbs.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.870
Oh, that’s right!

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.620
I got this really delicious bread.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.040
Would you like to try some?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.620
Uh, okay...

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:40.710
Thank y...

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.340
H-Huh?

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.140
There’s no need to hold back.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.560
Eat up.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.680
Umm...

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.520
Mother... I mean Your Majesty...

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.890
Wouldn’t you consider
reducing the amount of food you eat?

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.980
What are you talking about?

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:02.400
During pregnancy, you’re supposed to take in
plenty of nutrition for the baby inside you.

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:05.410
Actually, if you grow larger than you should be,

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:08.870
you could get toxemia or have a difficult delivery.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.410
It’s very dangerous to...

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:15.160
I believe I’ve heard that Mother died while birthing me...

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.460
Could it be that...

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.370
her obesity was the cause...?

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.220
What are you doing?

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.470
Give me back my comic meat.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:27.760
My queen...

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.090
The prince is saying that he’s full.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.140
When you become a world-level clown like me,

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:39.890
being able to hear the prince say that from within Your Majesty is a cinch.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.960
Oh, is that so?

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:42.680
Nod. Nod.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.030
I see. I see.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.610
Is he saying anything else?

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:46.860
Yep.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.860
The prince is saying that he really likes a slim and pretty mother.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.540
Oh, then I guess I should try dieting a little.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.290
Yes!

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.080
Hmm? Did you say something?

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.080
No, not at all.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:04.340
Then, I’ll talk to the chef and have the
menu changed over to a low-calorie menu.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.050
So, do your best for the prince, Your Majesty.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.170
Very well.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:10.980
Well then...

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:17.940
Your Majesty really listens to
anything that Pierrot-san tells you, right?

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:21.520
Well, if that’s what my child is saying...

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.070
That can’t be!

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.780
The child inside you can’t possibly talk, can he?

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.480
I guess that’s true.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.120
But, you know...

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:35.030
Somehow, I really felt like my
baby did say what Pierrot said.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.950
I wonder why...?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.370
<b>A few weeks later</b>

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.180
Oh yeah...

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.970
Today was a lot of fun, too.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.550
Mother’s lost weight and is beautiful again.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.060
So I guess I should return this ring to Mother.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.400
My hand is getting transparent?

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.440
Pierrot.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.980
Y-Your Majesty?

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.360
D-Did you need something?

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.120
I just wished to thank you.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.600
Thanks to you, the party was a big success.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:17.540
Thank you.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.540
N-Not at all.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.750
In addition to your world-level performances,

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:26.090
your cooking skills and sense of taste are outstanding.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.550
You can translate any foreign language...

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:32.300
And the garden that you sweep is always clean and shiny.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.550
You’re a really outstanding person!

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.300
You’re too kind.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:43.770
Both the king and I wish for this child to
become an outstanding person like you.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.440
Me?

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.810
Someone like me... is an outstanding person?

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.240
So, Pierrot...

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.780
I have a request.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.280
Please stay here forever.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.360
Would you take charge of
educating our soon-to-be-born child?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.370
Y-Your Majesty...

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.380
You have honored me with your generous words, but...

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.880
I guess it’s not possible, huh?

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:16.130
I’ve been sensing it for a long time.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.310
That one day you would leave us.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:21.850
I’m truly sorry.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:27.360
But, just promise me this.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:32.240
Until this child is born, please don’t go anywhere.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.750
Please.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.740
I’m sorry, Mother.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.880
I’d like to stay in this time forever, too.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:46.380
But soon, I’m going to have to return.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.760
That’s what this disappearing hand is telling me.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.380
M... Mother!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.480
Mother!

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.090
Oh no! Her water has broken!

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.730
But she’s not due yet!

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:03.600
Someone!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.600
Somebody come here!

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.190
It’s no good...

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.860
Everyone’s drunk from the party, so no one will come.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:13.150
At this rate, both the mother
and the child are in danger!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.110
An ambulance...

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.860
Oh, that won’t work...

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.820
It’ll take more than 15 minutes to get here!

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.540
She can’t wait that long!

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:24.500
I’ll go!

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.910
I’ll take her to the hospital!

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:38.180
We’re almost there, Mother!

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:39.420
We’re almost at the hospital!

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.600
Hurry, Pierrot.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.430
If you don’t hurry, both
Mother and the unborn child will...

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.270
What’s that?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.940
Pierrot’s moving his legs really fast!

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.190
You get the feeling that he’s in a real hurry.

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:56.940
I guess they’re running around in heaven.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.200
Huh?

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:01.240
Why did I want to send Pierrot to heaven?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.450
Was that really necessary?

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.040
I’m running out of... breath.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:13.460
I became a world-level clown
and I have a body that’s unmatched.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.800
So, why is it that at a time like this...

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.460
I’m losing my lungs?!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.000
But, I won’t lose!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.460
No matter how hard it is...

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.470
No matter how painful it is...

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.970
I will save this person for sure!

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.480
Pi... errot?

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:29.810
Mother!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.440
How can this be?!

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.110
The hospital is just an arm’s length away...

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:44.200
And my legs have disappeared...

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:48.320
I was finally able to meet my real
mother when she was still alive...

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:52.660
And after coming this far,
to think that I can’t save her life...

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:55.700
This is just... too cruel!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.590
Mother...

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:04.510
I’m sorry.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.850
Weep. Weep. Weep.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:16.730
Weep. Weep. Weeep.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.730
It seems like I’ve come back to my original time.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.530
It was a wonderful time travel.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.110
I could meet my mothe...

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.920
Why are you crying, son?

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.740
How pathetic.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:34.120
A crybaby like you will never be able
to compare to Pierrot Bolneze.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.830
M-M-Mother?!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.040
Why are you here?!

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.130
Exactly, Pierrot.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:46.930
We named you after the legendary clown
who saved the queen 23 years ago, and yet...

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.050
Father has come back to life, too!

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.890
If you start crying over judging a bread,
you still have a long way to go.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.770
Someday you have to take over
the crown of Monaco, and yet...

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:00.770
I guess we’re going to have to send
you back to Quedam Circus for training.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.520
Could it be that this is...

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:04.780
Father...

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.030
What is it?

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.570
This might sound silly, but...

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.360
According the custom of the Royal House of Monaco,

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:12.790
I was given away to the
household of some commoner, right?

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.780
The household of some commoner?!

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.290
You fool!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:19.240
You were entrusted to the care of the famous Quedam Circus

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.790
that the legendary Pierrot belonged to!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.800
The audience is... greatly reduced.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:27.800
There’s no mistake.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.680
At that time, Mother was probably saved by someone.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.590
And she gave birth to me safely.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.510
And hoping to meet the legendary Pierrot,

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.890
they must have entrusted me to the Quedam Circus.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.610
In other words... History has been changed!

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.940
The reason that there isn’t
much of an audience here is that...

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:48.360
I’m not the “miracle prince who
appeared 23 years later” anymore...

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.530
I’ve become just a regular prince.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.700
Right?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:53.870
Come on, Pierrot!

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.530
Stop making our guests wait!

00:14:56.530 --> 00:15:00.160
Once the reaction is over, you should announce the results immediately.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.460
Uh, yes! Right away.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.040
I didn’t know...

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.710
Both Mother and Father are the
kind who are strict with their son...

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.720
Well then, I’ll just announce the results.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.980
Azuma wins!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.770
What was that?!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.110
This Cannabis <i>Japan</i> is wonderful!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.360
No, awesome!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.490
No, not that!

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:31.820
How do I say this?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.240
This is a bread that cannot be described with words.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:39.250
If I were to still try to do so...
I’d call it a bread that can change history!

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:43.870
This bread is the ultimate bread that stands at the apex of all others!

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.080
The champions of the Second Monaco Cup are...

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.930
the Japanese representatives!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.050
Don’t mess with me, Pierrot.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:00.060
I sent you off to outer space!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.820
So, how could I lose?!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:08.270
It’s true that thanks to you I was able to meet
50,000 of my mothers who’d become a star.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:13.110
But, Azuma brought my real
mother and father back to life.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.990
What do you mean, a star?!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.410
What do you mean, brought back to life?!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.620
Both the king and the queen have always been here!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:23.660
The reason I sent you to space is... is...

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:25.000
Huh?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.670
What was it again?

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:30.670
With history having changed, it looks like these
people’s memories have been rewritten as well.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.340
The reason I made it doesn’t matter!

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.890
Explain why I lost!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.560
It’s the handmade flavor, Shadow-kun.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.310
K-Kirisaki...

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.730
Kirisaki? Is that the owner of St. Pierre?

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:50.150
Yes.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.150
You demon...

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:55.410
It was wonderful, Azuma Kazuma-kun.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.660
You completely went above and beyond me.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:02.910
That can’t be!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.670
It’s because you told me I would
become #1 in the world that I...

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.080
Listen carefully, Shadow...

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:11.090
The cannabis flour that Azuma-kun used...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.680
was flavored with an amazing brown sugar.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.680
It is called nabefuchi brown sugar.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:23.770
When sugar cane is boiled, sugar cane sap
slowly collects at the edges of the pot.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:28.600
Over time, it gets layered like a baumkuchen,
giving you the ultimate brown sugar.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.180
After repeating this process 20 times,

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:36.320
you get your first batch and you can scrape out just a little.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.990
This is something you have to make on your own.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:41.900
The natural sweetness of cannabis flour

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.950
and the deep flavor of the legendary nabefuchi brown sugar.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:49.500
It seems that the two of these together gave birth to the bread that can change history.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:55.510
But, we used legendary ingredients
like metzuru and Quality Season, too!

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:59.260
Ultimately, our ingredients were bought with money.

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:06.190
But, Azuma-kun worked hard to
make all the ingredients by himself.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.440
Also, during the manufacturing process,

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:14.030
Azuma-kun took the trouble to
bake it, fry it and bake it again.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:18.910
So, it’s obvious that his bread is better than ours.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.490
That’s right.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:26.330
Your food is delicious when you
think about the person who eats it,

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.710
and put time and effort into making it.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:35.340
The ultimate bread that you made for me...

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:40.720
helped fulfill my dream of meeting my father and mother.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.470
I really don’t know how to thank you.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.020
Huh? I can’t remember.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.480
I just can’t remember.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.480
Why did I work so hard?

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:54.490
#1 in the world...

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:56.860
My place as #1 in the world...

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.240
You’re being pathetic, Shadow.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.280
This is not the only chance you have.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:04.070
If you’re mad then aim for
the #1 spot in the world again.

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:07.950
And now, you should give
praise to that wonderful baker.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.080
Congratulations, Azuma Kazuma-kun.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:17.800
Congratulations.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.300
I’m sorry, but...

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:26.050
I can’t shake hands with you, old man.

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:27.940
Sorry.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.440
It started again, huh?

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:36.280
I must hurry.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:42.280
Umm... It kinda feels like Kirisaki is...

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:45.410
Not as much of a villain as we’d heard.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:48.160
That can’t be what you’re thinking, right?

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:52.580
He can’t show his real self here now, can he?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.290
I bet that once he realized he couldn’t win,

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:59.680
he judged that it was a better idea to show the world how magnanimous a man he is.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.460
How sportsman-like.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:03.380
Just as expected of the owner of St. Pierre.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.930
Yeah, it’s hard to be like that.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.590
You’re right!

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:11.600
In just a moment, it looks like rather
than us winning, we’ve been allowed to win.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:15.520
What a fearsome man Kirisaki Yuuichi is...

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.610
But, Azuma won!

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:21.900
If you make your bread with a will
and feelings stronger than anyone else,

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:26.620
it’s possible to defeat that man, who was
considered to be the #1 baker in the world.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.620
That was just proved!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.870
Well then.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.120
We’ll now start with the awards
ceremony for the Japanese representatives.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:35.670
Come to think of it...

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.210
What happened to Suwabara?

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.130
I’m... right here.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.130
Exactly when...?

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:43.800
I was feeling a little unwell.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.350
So, I was resting.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:50.310
He’d been feeling terrible ever
since we got off the helicopter...

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.180
Huh?

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:54.150
Come to think of it, why did we
need to ride in a helicopter anyway?

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:58.150
Once again, congratulations
to the Japanese representatives!

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.610
Well, we will now announce the MVP of this competition.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.900
Huh? Was there something like that?

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:06.650
My queen.

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:07.660
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.910
The MVP is the contestant Azuma Kazuma.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:15.380
The legendary ring of our Royal House,
the Pierron Ring, is presented to you.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.710
Oh! That’s...

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.420
Mother, didn’t you give that to me...?

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.300
What are you talking about?

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.880
I had given this ring to the legendary clown.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:29.140
It is not suitable for someone unworthy like you.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.640
Oh well, whatever.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:34.020
Come to think of it,

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.600
it was in order to meet Father and Mother

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:41.110
that I became the legendary clown and the judge of the Monaco Cup.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:48.030
Azuma fulfilled that wish of mine.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:52.540
I can’t possibly express my gratitude with just that ring.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.290
Azuma seems happy, too.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:59.580
This would just get in the way when I knead dough.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:00.920
I guess I’ll just give it to Tsukino.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:01.790
Treasure it.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:07.810
And so, all of the programs in the
Second Monaco Cup have been completed!

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:14.890
What are you...

00:22:15.470 --> 00:22:17.140
Let’s go, Kanmuri!

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:17.640
Tsukino!

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:19.730
Where are we going?

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:21.730
Isn’t that obvious?

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:23.240
Kawachi...

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:25.240
To toss our hero up in the air!

00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:07.100
We won the Monaco Cup!

00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:08.400
Roar!

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:11.020
But, I’m having a bad premonition, Manager...

00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:13.870
Yeah, I can’t imagine that that man would back off.

00:24:13.870 --> 00:24:15.370
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.370 --> 00:24:16.830
A Letter of Challenge from Kirisaki!!

00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:18.870
The start of a new program, Yakitate!! 9!

00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:19.860
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:22.610
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.050
Sugar cane is also known as kansha.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:27.470
It’s a perennial plant of the family Gramineae.

00:24:27.470 --> 00:24:30.300
It grows in areas where the year-round temperatures are above 20°C.

00:24:30.300 --> 00:24:31.630
Viva Okinawa!

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:34.350
Oh?!
